            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0391" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg379"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.24/331</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Adviser on
                        Political Relations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Duggan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-02-17">February 17, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Duggan</hi>: I have spoken personally with
                    Admiral Stark. He is instructing Captain Spears not to sign any written
                    agreement and <pb facs="0392" n="380" xml:id="pg380"/> not to have the
                    Argentines sign any written agreement. Their recommendations will consequently
                    be merely regarded as having been formulated for submission to the Chief of
                    Naval Operations. I think you better make sure that the War Department follows
                    the lead of the Navy Department in this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">elles</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
